    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 81.88 score. His matchup against Bello is highly favorable, bolstered by an 8% boost from an elite 25-PA BvP historical edge and a strong +14% platoon adjustment. Following closely is **Kyle Tucker**, whose 75.93 rating against Nelson reflects a clean profile, benefiting from his prime cleanup spot and solid park factors. **Andy Pages** also earns a strong recommendation at 66.22; while he faces the same pitcher as **Kyle Tucker**, his placement in the three-hole provides the optimal environment to capitalize on high-leverage counting stats.\n\nThe middle of our lineup requires more caution. **Jackson Merrill** holds a marginal 51.97 score, heavily suppressed by a -19% SP skill penalty against Wheeler, one of the premier arms in the league. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.26) sees his upside capped by a matchup against the crafty Sale, though he remains in the lineup due to his reliable base projection. **Coby Mayo** and **Brayan Rocchio** are our most volatile starts today, hovering near the 50-point threshold. **Miguel Andujar** was the primary consideration for a bench promotion; however, his score of 34.66 fell well below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor,\" as the combination of facing Wheeler\u2019s elite stuff and an unfavorable platoon split kept him firmly on the bench. \n\nInvestors should monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, who remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our bench depth tested. With **Jackson Merrill** facing a pitcher who effectively limits stolen base opportunities, we are sacrificing our typical appetite for speed in favor of raw production, necessitating a high-floor performance from our core hitters to remain competitive in the 5x5 categories. We are currently navigating these matchups without the services of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, or **Liam Hicks**, who remain unavailable for this specific deployment.",
